PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: Your body is severely intolerant to salicylates, chemicals naturally found in many healthy foods like berries and mint, as well as in aspirin. Eating them caused a massive release of inflammatory chemicals that choked your airways and inflamed your skin.
Actionable Steps: Take the antihistamine to stop the hives. Use your inhaler if the wheezing returns. You must strictly avoid all berries, almonds, mint, and any anti-inflammatory painkillers (like Nurofen or Aspirin) to prevent another life-threatening flare.

